# FLOW: student invites -> receptionist approves -> check-out
# Before you run: you need  {{rec1Token}} (receptionist, building 1)  and  {{emiliaToken}} (active student WITH a room in building 1).
# Run top to bottom. Write the status of each step.
#
# SQL before: Emilia must have an active reservation.
#   SELECT s.Id, s.FirstName, r.Id AS ResId, r.RoomId, r.Status FROM Students s
#   LEFT JOIN Reservations r ON r.StudentId = s.Id WHERE s.FirstName = 'Emilia';
#   (Reservations.Status 0 = Active)
# Also note the room occupancy:  SELECT Id, CurrentOccupancy, Capacity FROM Rooms;

### 1) Emilia invites a guest                               # EXPECT 200, status Pending
@emiliaToken = eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..Z3CMkdYGYXIVWwn9FWZmJeGHScKZSl3DMpi3tz1PWzY

# @name invite
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/app/myinvitation/create
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{emiliaToken}}

{ "GuestFullName": "Karim Test", "GuestDocumentNumber": "KT100200", "DocumentType": "Passport" }

{{
  exports.invitationId = response.parsedBody.payload.id;
}}

### 2) Emilia invites AGAIN (same month)                    # EXPECT 409, and NO new guest in SQL
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/app/myinvitation/create
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{emiliaToken}}

{ "GuestFullName": "Second Guest", "GuestDocumentNumber": "SG300400", "DocumentType": "Passport" }

### 3) Receptionist sees only the Pending ones    
@piotrToken = eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..lsvWnVMNtRyHTBD6ggxdeXgjzTJ39gaLSdJ7Aw4j0g8
@rec1Token =eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..adYv3VJCtubwSMtHnr7ZyueYcN1R8wu-ynk4Cvn-S0A
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/invitation/get-all
Authorization: Bearer {{rec1Token}}
X-Building-Id: 1

### 4) Receptionist approves                                # EXPECT 200, status Used, reservationId filled
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/invitation/approve/3
Authorization: Bearer {{rec1Token}}
X-Building-Id: 1

### 5) Approve the SAME invitation again                    # EXPECT 409 "must be pending"
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/invitation/approve/3
Authorization: Bearer {{rec1Token}}
X-Building-Id: 1

### 6) Approve an invitation that does not exist            # EXPECT 404
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/invitation/approve/99999
Authorization: Bearer {{rec1Token}}
X-Building-Id: 1

### 7) Approve with a token of another building             # EXPECT 403 (header 2) 
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/invitation/approve/3
Authorization: Bearer {{rec1Token}}
X-Building-Id: 2

### 8) Student token on the approve endpoint                # EXPECT 403
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/invitation/approve/3
Authorization: Bearer {{emiliaToken}}
X-Building-Id: 1

### 9) Find the new reservation id (see SQL below), then check-out.
# SQL: SELECT Id, Type, Status, RoomId, TotalAmount FROM Reservations WHERE InvitationId = <invitationId>;
# Expected: Type InvitationStay (2), Status 0, TotalAmount 0, RoomId = Emilia's room.
# Room occupancy must be UNCHANGED:  SELECT Id, CurrentOccupancy FROM Rooms WHERE Id = <RoomId>;
